    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0318" n="1052" xml:id="pg1052"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hices to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September 2, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 421.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Neill’s No. 407, of July
                    27, 1892, and my Nos. 355, of April 1, and 357, of April 8, 1892, I have to say
                    that in view of the action of the representatives of England, France, Germany,
                    Spain, and Italy, in jointly urging upon the Peruvian Government the necessity
                    of paying the just claims of citizens of those Governments, I deemed it best
                    once more to call the attention of the Government to the claims known as that of
                    the Hydrographic Commission.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, on this date I forwarded to the minister of foreign affairs a note
                    on the subject, and I inclose herewith a copy of the same.</p>
                <p>In expressing the hope that something may come of it I can not refrain also from
                    saying that I have but little confidence that it will be immediately paid. The
                    Peruvian Government is not paying any of its creditors, as I have heretofore
                    explained.</p>
                <p>Your, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hicks.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
